// the asymmetry the whole interface design rests on: a struct's conformance is a compile-time contract
// and nothing more. it has no block and no identity word, so there is no runtime answer to give - which
// is CONCEPT.md's "you can also not perform any runtime reflection checks on them" applied to interfaces

interface Drawable
{
    function draw() : void;
}

struct Square : Drawable
{
    float64 $side;

    function draw() : void {
        echo 1;
    }
}

$square = Square(2.0);

// the conformance is real and usable through a constraint - it is only `instanceof` that cannot answer
echo $square instanceof Drawable;
